  "intent": {
    "user_prompt": "Build an 8-bit streaming accumulator datapath as a complete SR2FPGA Verilog RTL project. This is component topology t2_stream_accumulator, difficulty tier T2. Use a skid_buffer feeding an accumulator_core. The design must implement this black-box behavior: valid input samples pass through a skid buffer and accumulate into the running sum. Keep rtl/top.v as the integration wrapper and keep each reusable component in a separate RTL file. Preserve these interface contracts: top.in_valid -> skid_buffer.in_valid; top.in_data -> skid_buffer.in_data; skid_buffer.out_valid -> accumulator_core.sample_valid; skid_buffer.out_data -> accumulator_core.sample; accumulator_core.sample_ready -> skid_buffer.out_ready; accumulator_core.sum -> top.sum. Include system_his.json, manifest.json, timing constraints, predicted QoR, and a bounded self-checking testbench that prints TEST_PASS only on success or TEST_FAIL on failure.",
    "design_goal": "Implement an 8‑bit streaming accumulator using a skid buffer for decoupling and an accumulator core.",
    "assumptions": [
      "8‑bit unsigned arithmetic with wrap‑around on overflow.",
      "Active‑low synchronous reset initializes sum to zero and clears buffer state.",
      "The skid buffer provides a single‑stage pipeline for handshake decoupling.",
      "Output sample_valid is asserted when a new accumulated sum is available."
    ]
  },
